  "id": "automatic-thoughts",
  "term": "automatic thoughts",
  "definition": "In this source, automatic thoughts are described as immediate, hard-to-control negative judgments about oneself, the environment, and the future. They may appear as distorted thinking patterns such as overgeneralizing, catastrophizing, self-blame, black-and-white thinking, or dismissing positive experiences.",
